      "description": "GLM47 Coach has a land drop available (Forest, Ghost Quarter, or Ugin's Labyrinth) and chose to pass without playing one. They have Sowing Mycospawn in hand which costs {3}{G} with kicker {1}{C}, and accelerating mana is important for casting it next turn (potentially kicked). Playing Forest would provide an additional green source, and there's no reason to hold it since it enters untapped. Missing a land drop when you have lands in hand and expensive spells to cast is a clear mistake.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without playing a land, despite having Forest, Ghost Quarter, and Ugin's Labyrinth in hand.",
