      "snapshot_index": 174,
      "player": "GLM47 Coach",
      "decision_index": 128,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "GLM47 Coach chose to exile Teferi, Time Raveler instead of Wrenn and Six with Ugin's cast trigger. Teferi is at 1 loyalty and can only bounce/draw once more before dying, while Wrenn and Six is at 4 loyalty and provides recurring land recursion (fueling Phlage escapes and fixing) and threatens an ultimate. Wrenn and Six is the more impactful long-term threat. However, Teferi's static ability prevents Coach from casting spells at instant speed (each opponent can cast spells only any time they could cast a sorcery), which matters less now that Ugin is resolving. Teferi also could bounce Ugin with its -3, which would be devastating. That said, Teferi at 1 loyalty is very fragile and Gramps' lands are all tapped, so the bounce threat isn't immediate. Wrenn at 4 loyalty is much harder to remove and provides more sustained value.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Teferi, Time Raveler (1 loyalty) with Ugin's cast trigger",
      "better_line": "Exile Wrenn and Six (4 loyalty), which is a more durable and impactful threat. Teferi at 1 loyalty could be dealt with by Ugin's ongoing triggered ability on the next colorless spell, or would die to any incidental damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 217,
      "player": "GLM47 Coach",
      "decision_index": 153,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Exiled fetch lands (Arid Mesa, 2x Flooded Strand) from graveyard for Phlage's escape cost while Wrenn and Six is on the battlefield at 4 loyalty, capable of recurring those fetch lands every turn for repeated landfall triggers and mana fixing.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Arid Mesa and both Flooded Strands (valuable Wrenn and Six recursion targets) as part of Phlage's escape cost.",
      "better_line": "Exile cards with no graveyard utility instead, such as Solitude, Malevolent Rumble, Prismatic Ending, Forest, and Delighted Halfling, preserving fetch lands for Wrenn and Six's +1 ability to generate recurring value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 251,
      "player": "Grok4F Gramps",
      "decision_index": 170,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GLM47 Coach passed without playing Ghost Quarter from hand, missing a free land drop. With Emrakul, the Promised End in hand costing 8 mana (13 minus 5 card types in graveyard), every land matters. Ghost Quarter also could potentially destroy an opponent's land or simply provide colorless mana next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without playing Ghost Quarter or activating Ugin's Labyrinth.",
      "better_line": "Play Ghost Quarter as the land for the turn to advance toward casting Emrakul. Could also activate the untapped Ugin's Labyrinth to return Ugin, Eye of the Storms to hand for future use.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 267,
      "player": "GLM47 Coach",
      "decision_index": 180,
    }
  ],
